classDiagram
  direction TB
  accTitle: Simplified DOT domain model
  accDescr: Dot declares Contracts and contains Connectors and Runtime alternatives. A Connector selects a Contract operation. Each Runtime offers Deployments. A Deployment contains one manifest and its logical services. A separate Composition aggregate owns vertices that select exact DOT releases. Edges connect vertices and contain channels that select their connectors.

  class Dot
  class Contract
  class Connector
  class Runtime
  class Deployment
  class Manifest {
    <<abstract>>
  }
  class Service
  class Composition
  class Vertex
  class Edge
  class Channel

  Composition *-- Vertex : vertices
  Composition *-- Edge : edges
  Vertex ..> Dot : references
  Edge ..> Vertex : from / to
  Edge *-- Channel : channels
  Vertex ..> Connector : selects IDs
  Channel ..> Connector : selects endpoints
  Dot --> Contract : declares
  Dot *-- Connector : connectors
  Dot *-- Runtime : runtimes
  Connector ..> Contract : selects operation
  Runtime *-- Deployment : alternatives
  Deployment *-- Manifest : manifest
  Deployment *-- Service : services
